<div class="bard-content bard-box light-grey">
    
    <p><strong>Age Recommendation: </strong>14+</p><p>Everyone, regardless of age, must have their own ticket to enter the theatre. Children under the age of 16 must be accompanied by, and seated next to, a ticketholder who is at least 18 years old. Children under the age of 3 will not be admitted.</p><p><strong>Please note: </strong>This production contains haze, short moments of strobe lighting and adult themes. For more content information please <a href="https://dirtydancingonstage.co.uk/london/">click here</a></p>
    
</div>



                        
                            
    <div class="bard-content !mb-0">
        
        <p><strong>Performance Schedule</strong></p><p><span style="color: black;">Monday – Thursday: 7.30pm</span><br><span style="color: black;">Friday: 5pm &amp; 8.30pm</span><br><span style="color: black;">Saturday: 2.30pm &amp; 7.30pm</span></p><p><strong><span style="color: black;">Show Running Time: </span></strong><span style="color: black;">Approximately 2 hours 15 minutes including an interval.</span></p>
    </div>
    

                        
                            

<div class="bard-content bard-box light-grey">
    
    <p>Latecomers may not be admitted until a suitable break, but we cannot guarantee admittance into the performance.<br>If you need to leave your seat during the performance, you may be asked to wait until a suitable moment before re-entering the auditorium. This is to minimise disturbance both to other audience members and the performers on stage.<br><strong>Please note that you may not bring food or drink purchased elsewhere into our theatres.</strong><br>The producers may make alterations to the published cast for any reason, at any time, and therefore cannot guarantee the appearance of any named artist.<br>Filming, photography and phone use are not permitted during the performance.<br>For full terms and conditions, please <a href="/terms-and-conditions"><u>click here</u></a>.</p>
    
</div>
